{{!-- The answer: how long the journey takes, by which legs, and what that ticked on Chart a Course.

      Shared by the route step and the "See the whole map" window, so the number the GM reads is the
      same wherever they happen to be looking. Context is the journey object. --}}
{{#if journey.route}}
<div class="stonetop-journey-route">
  {{!-- WHY THE MAP ABOVE HAS NO LINE ON IT. `routePath` will not bridge a missing END of a
        journey, for the reason set out over it, and six of the places the books letter are drawn
        on the Vicinity alone. So choosing one and then opening the World&rsquo;s End took the whole
        route line away with nothing on screen saying so, and the map read as having forgotten the
        trip rather than as being unable to draw it.

        It sits with the READOUT rather than over the picture because the readout is the half that
        still answers, and because both surfaces draw this partial: the route step sets it under
        its map, the window under its viewport. --}}
  {{#if journey.map.offMap}}
  <p class="stonetop-journey-offmap">
    <i class="fas fa-map-location-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    {{!-- The sentence is written in ExpeditionDialog._offMapReadout, off the same en.json keys the
          refusal toast uses, so the two cannot come to say different things about one fact. All
          this partial owns is the button. --}}
    {{journey.map.offMap.sentence}}
    {{#if journey.map.offMap.other}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-journey-elsewhere" data-tier="{{journey.map.offMap.other}}">
      {{journey.map.offMap.showLabel}}
    </button>
    {{/if}}
  </p>
  {{/if}}
  {{!-- "at least 7-8 days" for the table's own times, "roughly 4-6 days" for a way measured off
        the map. One is a floor the book printed and the other is a good guess; `routePhrase` is
        what tells them apart, and the class lets the estimate carry its own mark. --}}
  <div class="stonetop-journey-total{{#if journey.route.estimated}} is-estimate{{/if}}">{{journey.route.atLeast}}</div>
  <ol class="stonetop-journey-legs">
    {{#each journey.route.legs}}
    {{!-- A leg the table prices keeps its printed time and its road, on a hand-drawn way as much as
          on a solved one. An estimated leg wears the tilde, so a reader can see at a glance which
          half of a mixed answer the book stands behind. A leg with no time at all is one this map
          cannot place an end of; it still says where it runs. --}}
    <li{{#if estimated}} class="is-estimate"{{/if}}>
      <span class="j-from">{{fromName}}</span>
      <span class="j-arw">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="j-to">{{toName}}</span>
      {{#if time}}<b class="j-time">{{#if estimated}}~{{/if}}{{time}}</b>{{/if}}
      {{#if via}}<em class="j-via">by {{via}}</em>{{/if}}
    </li>
    {{/each}}
  </ol>
  {{#if journey.route.estimated}}
  {{!-- WHERE THE NUMBER CAME FROM, because a GM about to tell the table "at least six days" is
        owed the difference between a figure the book printed and one this system measured. The
        derivation is in utils/custom-route.js `tierPace`; this is its one-line summary. --}}
  <p class="stonetop-journey-estimate">
    <i class="fas fa-ruler" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    {{journey.route.estimateNote}}
  </p>
  {{/if}}
  {{!-- What the route actually carried onto the checklist, and nothing it did not. `hasStops` is
        about intermediate stops alone, so leaning on it for the days as well told the GM the days
        were filled in on every single-leg journey — including the four measured only in hours,
        where the blank stays empty and the box stays unticked. --}}
  {{#if journey.route.hasStops}}
  <p class="stonetop-journey-note">
    Ticked on <strong>Chart a Course</strong>: they must first travel to
    {{#each journey.route.stops}}<strong>{{this}}</strong>{{#unless @last}}, then {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{#if journey.route.hasDays}}, with the days filled in{{/if}}.
  </p>
  {{else if journey.route.hasDays}}
  <p class="stonetop-journey-note">Ticked on <strong>Chart a Course</strong>, with the days filled in.</p>
  {{else}}
  <p class="stonetop-journey-note">
    Under a day's walk, so <strong>Chart a Course</strong> has no blank this route can fill.
  </p>
  {{/if}}
</div>
{{/if}}
